# DEFECT 078: `owned` on an out-parameter the header spells `const char **`
# stopped the build with `internal error`, exit 2 (panel 175's spec-warden,
# 2026-09-23).
#
# SYMPTOM: `check` 0, then `internal error: compiling the generated C failed`
# around clang's own sentence, *passing 'char **' to parameter of type 'const
# char **' discards qualifiers in nested pointer types* — the compiler blaming
# itself for the author's declaration, on Darwin and both Linux legs.
#
# CAUSE: the `char **` carve-out in `emit/ffi_mutable.hero` stepped aside for
# every `owned` cell, so clang's refusal of the const one reached nobody who
# could read it.
#
# FIX (panel 176, question 4, its resolution's item 8): the carve-out steps
# aside for a header that says `char **` and reports `ffi_owned_const_cell`
# for one that says `const char **`. The header's const says C lends; the mark
# says C gives; only the author can say which is true, so the note offers both
# repairs and no fix is `certain`.
extern "ffi-owned-on-a-cell-the-header-spells-const.h"
    function fill_out(@out: cstr owned free_out)  #~ ffi_owned_const_cell
    function free_out(p: cstr)

function main()
    s: str? @= fail(code: "none", msg: "nothing yet")
    fill_out(out: @s)
    print("after")
